phase P10
title Release
description
    **Class:** verifiable.

    **Kind:** ticket.

    **Goal:**

    - the package published, only as far as the user asks;
    - its published name decided then.

    **Starts when:** P9's completion audit passes.

    **Verified by:**

    - the packed-consumer check on the exact tarball;
    - `nub run verify`;
    - an independent review of the release change.

    **One iteration:** implement, check independently, repair.

    **Exit criteria:** acceptance passes at the final revision, and each requested ship stage is
    confirmed by the user.

    **False pass:** publishing a package whose installed form differs from what was tested.

    **Caught by:** the packed-consumer check.

    **Gates:** the packed-consumer check, which rejects a tarball packed with one entry point
    removed.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:** before each ship stage (publish, land, tag); the published name.

    **Draws from:** skill:playbook-ship; skill:review.
tasks
    T50
        title       Package routes and installed form
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@task.V3.T23]
        satisfies   [@plan.FlowState.O2, @plan.Package.O1, @plan.Package.O2, @plan.Package.O3]
        description
            Build the six package routes, peers, `sideEffects`, removed surfaces and InvalidConfiguration help, and
            run the packed-consumer check from T23 onward.

            **Why now:** no Task builds @plan.Package.O1 to O3, and @plan.FlowState.O2 wants the packed-consumer
            check at every stage gate, but only T39 runs it, at release.

            **Read first:** @plan.Package.O1, @plan.Package.O2, @plan.Package.O3, @plan.Package.D1,
            @plan.FlowState.O2.

            **Approach:** six closed routes via `exports`, ESM only, no deep import (K01); the root export list and
            a root that imports no React, server, Node, testing or inspect code (K02, K04); server route conditions
            and the ServerOnlyImport stub (K03); Effect peer exactly 4.0.5, React optional peer 18 and 19 (K05);
            `sideEffects: false` (K06); packed declarations keep inference (K07); removed surfaces without aliases
            (K08); InvalidConfiguration with replacement help (K09).

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/package.json`, its build config and the packed-consumer check.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** routes that resolve in the workspace but not from a tarball → caught by the
              packed-consumer check.
            - **Gates:** the packed-consumer check, which rejects a tarball packed with one route removed.
            - **Stops:** public entry-point names.
        acceptance
            - The six routes resolve from an installed tarball and nothing else does (@plan.Package.O1).
            - Peers, `sideEffects`, removed surfaces and InvalidConfiguration help are checked on the tarball
              (@plan.Package.O2, @plan.Package.O3).
            - The packed-consumer check runs at each stage gate from T23 onward.
    T39
        title       Release as far as the user asks
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@T50]
        description
            Release the package as far as the user asks: pack, run the packed-consumer check, and stop before each ship
            stage.

            **Why now:** the release is the last step of the epic, and what ships must be the form that was tested.

            **Read first:** @plan.Package.O4, @plan.Package.D1, skill:playbook-ship, skill:review.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** tested form differs from published → caught by the packed-consumer
              check.
            - **Gates:** the packed-consumer check.
            - **Stops:** each ship stage; the published name.
        acceptance
            The packed-consumer check passes on the exact tarball; each requested stage done.
